{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/156971-homebrew-demonic-merits","id":156971,"title":"Homebrew Demonic Merits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-02T16:03:00-07:00","id":156971,"title":"Homebrew Demonic Merits","content":"I figured there should be someplace for everyone's Homebrew Demonic Merits so here it is. (Hopefully there hasn't already been one created)<br /> <br /> <br /> Here's mine:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Electronic Counter Measures E.C.M</b> (2 - 3 Dots)<br /> <br /> A Demon's Cover has an instinctual ability to cover up vaguely supernatural occurrences that would occur around a Demon's Cover that a Demon can Spoof. This is a great counter-measure for supernatural detection but it is not full proof. There are some unchained that have a natural afinity for spoof supernatural senses. This ability, sometimes called <b>White Noise</b>, acts like an electronic emission that cancels out the senses when it feels scrutiny. This make the Unchained harder to spot as supernatural and bolsters the Demon's ability to <b>Spoof</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Effect: </b>At two dots, White Noise emits a low frequency wave that adds a +1 bonus to Spoof. At three dots, the Demon gains a +2 bonus on <b>Spoof</b> rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T16:39:15-07:00","id":157049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/156971-homebrew-demonic-merits#post156971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figured there should be someplace for everyone's Homebrew Demonic Merits so here it is. (Hopefully there hasn't already been one created)<br /> <br /> <br /> Here's mine:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Electronic Counter Measures E.C.M</b> (2 - 3 Dots)<br /> <br /> A Demon's Cover has an instinctual ability to cover up vaguely supernatural occurrences that would occur around a Demon's Cover that a Demon can Spoof. This is a great counter-measure for supernatural detection but it is not full proof. There are some unchained that have a natural afinity for spoof supernatural senses. This ability, sometimes called <b>White Noise</b>, acts like an electronic emission that cancels out the senses when it feels scrutiny. This make the Unchained harder to spot as supernatural and bolsters the Demon's ability to <b>Spoof</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Effect: </b>At two dots, White Noise emits a low frequency wave that adds a +1 bonus to Spoof. At three dots, the Demon gains a +2 bonus on <b>Spoof</b> rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Home On Jam - HOJ</b> (2 Dots)<br /> <br /> The Demon can sense when someone is using ECM. Gain a +2 bonus on rolls to identify and track someone using ECM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T09:30:05-07:00","id":160025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/156971-homebrew-demonic-merits?p=157049#post157049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <b>Home On Jam - HOJ</b> (2 Dots)<br /> <br /> The Demon can sense when someone is using ECM. Gain a +2 bonus on rolls to identify and track someone using ECM.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was it really that bad? :/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T23:19:29-07:00","id":164550,"title":"","content":"HoJ is a real thing used to defeat certain types of ECM; I was being tongue-in-cheek, not critical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T07:21:20-07:00","id":164816,"title":"","content":"<b>Sample-Replication Chamber</b> (5 Dots)<br /> The SRC is the ultimate in spoofing, in that it spoofs the Universe to replicate the abilities of a sample placed into it. Granted to Angels designed to infiltrate supernatural communities, this modification (also available as a Process), the Angel/Unchained is able to replicate one capability exhibited by another supernatural. A sample from one supernatural whose ability is to be replicated must be obtained and placed within the chamber, and then the fine-tuning begins. This sample could be harvested from a corpse or bargained away as part of a Pact (in which case the original Supernatural cannot do it unless they recover it). Samples harvested from a corpse are much harder to fine-tune, requiring more time, but can be done in a week or so. Corpses older than a month are useless for this.<br /> <br /> Examples of abilities that can be replicated include:<br /> * A Werewolf's Gift<br /> * One of a Werewolf's forms (Hishu/Dalu/Gauru/Urshul/Urhan)<br /> * One entry of a Changeling's Contract<br /> * A Changeling's Mein<br /> * A Changeling's Kith-ability<br /> * A Mage's proficiency with one Practice of one Arcana<br /> * A Mage's Attainment<br /> <br /> The SRC can store up to two units of the essences powering these abilities (Essence/Mana/Plasm/Pyros/Etc.), but locating these essences is up to the Angel/Unchained.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T05:25:27-07:00","id":165825,"title":"","content":"Every Demon would want the Death Arcana's / Tremere's soul thef ability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T13:54:51-07:00","id":166213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paddon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/156971-homebrew-demonic-merits?p=164816#post164816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Sample-Replication Chamber</b> (5 Dots)<br /> The SRC is the ultimate in spoofing, in that it spoofs the Universe to replicate the abilities of a sample placed into it. Granted to Angels designed to infiltrate supernatural communities, this modification (also available as a Process), the Angel/Unchained is able to replicate one capability exhibited by another supernatural. A sample from one supernatural whose ability is to be replicated must be obtained and placed within the chamber, and then the fine-tuning begins. This sample could be harvested from a corpse or bargained away as part of a Pact (in which case the original Supernatural cannot do it unless they recover it). Samples harvested from a corpse are much harder to fine-tune, requiring more time, but can be done in a week or so. Corpses older than a month are useless for this.<br /> <br /> Examples of abilities that can be replicated include:<br /> * A Werewolf's Gift<br /> * One of a Werewolf's forms (Hishu/Dalu/Gauru/Urshul/Urhan)<br /> * One entry of a Changeling's Contract<br /> * A Changeling's Mein<br /> * A Changeling's Kith-ability<br /> * A Mage's proficiency with one Practice of one Arcana<br /> * A Mage's Attainment<br /> <br /> The SRC can store up to two units of the essences powering these abilities (Essence/Mana/Plasm/Pyros/Etc.), but locating these essences is up to the Angel/Unchained.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not have it give them 3-4 dots in Dark Powers? Would work out a <i>lot</i> better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T15:54:18-07:00","id":166301,"title":"","content":"Actually, thinking about it a bit more, I think that <b>Sample-Replication Chamber</b> would make a pretty great Process. Just make it less permanent and it would be pretty cool for a demon game that cross-overs a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T07:14:15-07:00","id":167890,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I'd model this more after the refinement of silver ability in promethean, or the 'make a cover out of spirits or ghosts&quot; power.<br /> <br /> So the demon could make a vampire cover, be able to pass as a vampire and notice vampires, but I'd be real hesitant to allow them to use another splat's powers. I would allow them to use their own abilities: demon form advantages, embeds, and exploits as if they were the splat in question. So a demon could use that power to move anything or that ability to knock anyone out in one punch and call it vigor and lo and behold not a cover compromise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T12:07:47-07:00","id":168154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/156971-homebrew-demonic-merits?p=165825#post165825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every Demon would want the Death Arcana's / Tremere's soul thef ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wrong use of &quot;Soul&quot; in Soul Pact. A Demon with their hands on just a Soul wouldn't be able to use it any more than a mundane human. They need the mind attached to it to make bargains with. A Demon's Soul Pact isn't for their SOUL, it's for their place in the Grand Scheme Of Things, for their galactic coordinates in the cosmos, for their seat on the boat going down the river Styx, for their particular thread of Fate. Every Demon would want the Fate Arcana's purview of coincidence, however, to ensure their contracts happen correctly or they approach their mark when the mark is the most receptive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T12:09:43-07:00","id":168178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/156971-homebrew-demonic-merits?p=166301#post166301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, thinking about it a bit more, I think that <b>Sample-Replication Chamber</b> would make a pretty great Process. Just make it less permanent and it would be pretty cool for a demon game that cross-overs a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I initially designed it with it being a Process, but jury-rigged it to be a Merit for the sake of this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T12:17:54-07:00","id":168193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/156971-homebrew-demonic-merits?p=166213#post166213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why not have it give them 3-4 dots in Dark Powers? Would work out a <i>lot</i> better.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could certainly work! I'm just approaching Demon: the Descent with experience in other venues, but you could certainly just say &quot;4 dots in Dread Powers, but get a sample from something that has those Dread Powers.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T23:32:04-07:00","id":170447,"title":"","content":"The following was inspired by the Virtuous and Vice-Ridden Merits.<br /> <br /> <b>Deeper Than Skin</b> (\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Cover Rating of 6+<br /> This Merit represents a Demon really being able to &quot;get into character&quot; with a particular Cover. For two dots, the Demon selects a second Virtue <i>or</i> Vice. For four dots, the Demon selects both a Virtue and Vice. While using the Cover this Merit is assigned to, the Demon can recover Willpower using either of its Virtues or Vices, and can even &quot;mix and match&quot;. All other rules regarding Virtue and Vice apply.<br /> This Merit is assigned to a specific Cover when purchased. If that Cover's rating drops below six, the Demon has become sufficiently detached from the Cover and no longer benefits from the additional Virtue/Vice until it repairs the Cover. Should the Cover be destroyed, all rules regarding Cover-specific Merits apply.<br /> This Merit can be bought multiple times but only once for any given Cover. A Demon can start with the two-dot version and later upgrade to the four-dot if desired.<br /> <br /> Edit: An equivalent to this Merit is presented on page 149 of <i>Flowers of Hell</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The Man and the Beast are having an amiable picnic in that Savage\u2019s head. It\u2019s rather disturbing.&quot; <i>- Blood and Smoke: the Strix Chronicle, pg. 22</i>","edited":{"userid":145,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/145-jsm3050","user":"JSM3050","date":". 07-03-2014, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/145-jsm3050","name":"JSM3050","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T00:21:49-07:00","id":171476,"title":"","content":"Partial Transformation (4 points I guess): You can adopt features from one cover while in another cover.<br /> <br /> For most demons, this is just a useful disguise ability: Assume one cover, adapt the height of another cover, and the coloring of another, and so on.<br /> <br /> For demons with more exotic covers, this becomes even more useful, turning your hand into a sword, or replacing your feet with car wheels, or manifesting a cyberarm in bleeding edge, or alien features in infinite macabre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T14:27:46-07:00","id":180085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/156971-homebrew-demonic-merits?p=167890#post167890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hmm, I'd model this more after the refinement of silver ability in promethean, or the 'make a cover out of spirits or ghosts&quot; power.<br /> So the demon could make a vampire cover, be able to pass as a vampire and notice vampires, but I'd be real hesitant to allow them to use another splat's powers. I would allow them to use their own abilities: demon form advantages, embeds, and exploits as if they were the splat in question. So a demon could use that power to move anything or that ability to knock anyone out in one punch and call it vigor and lo and behold not a cover compromise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been waiting almost two weeks to respond to this but couldn't because Flowers wasn't out yet (NDA and all), but you might want to check out Flowers of Hell. It includes an Embed and an Exploit intended to scratch the itch for people who want their demon characters to go undercover among other supernatural groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T00:05:02-07:00","id":181730,"title":"","content":"Yes, I saw that, and for an exploit I can't really argue that it's unreasonable, allowing demons to use disciplines et al but as a merit? Still think that's too much for a merit.<br /> <br /> Heck, I wouldn't have minded if the &quot;make an ephemeral cover&quot; exploit had allowed one to use influences and numina as part of the package, but I guess those demons will just have to buy another exploit to fully pull of the &quot;hey look at me I'm a tree spirit&quot; thing work. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}